<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vajrayana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tantric Buddhism, Esoteric Buddhism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vajrayana, or Tantric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, is a form of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism">Mahayana Buddhism</a> that developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from around the 7th century, using ritual, mantras, mandalas and initiation by a teacher to seek rapid enlightenment. It spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> and maritime South-East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, where Javanese and Sumatran kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adityawarman">Adityawarman</a> combined it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a> in royal cult and temple building.</p></div>
